Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: klipr
Upstream-Contact: Nguyen Duc <nguyenminhduc230903@gmail.com>
Source: https://github.com/NguyenDuc2309/klipr
Comment:
 The upstream git tree carries a self-hosted APT repository under landing/apt,
 used to serve the project's own .deb builds from GitHub Pages. It is committed
 to git and so appears in the tarball GitHub generates for a tag, but it holds
 prebuilt binaries (a .deb pool, a dearmoured keyring and signed index files)
 that have no place in a Debian source package. The whole directory is dropped,
 along with any byte-compiled Python caches and stray build output; this is why
 the upstream version carries a +ds suffix.
Files-Excluded:
 landing/apt
 */__pycache__
 *.pyc
 klipr_*.deb

